{"id":"longest-running-tv","title":"Longest-running US network TV series","prompt":"Name the 10 scripted primetime series on US broadcast networks (ABC, CBS, NBC, Fox, The CW) with the most seasons","noun":"TV series","category":"Entertainment","metric":"Seasons","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of longest-running scripted American primetime television series","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_longest-running_scripted_American_primetime_television_series","asOf":"2026-11-04"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"The Simpsons","aliases":["TV Simpsons","Simpson","Simpsons TV show","The simsons","The simppsons","Sympsons"],"value":"38 seasons","n":38,"article":"The Simpsons","fact":{"text":"Matt Groening named the family after his own, putting in Bart for himself; \"Simpson\" sounded like \"simpleton\".","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Simpsons"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Law & Order: Special Victims Unit","aliases":["Special Victims Unit","Law And Order SVU","SVU"],"value":"28 seasons","n":28,"article":"Law & Order: Special Victims Unit","fact":{"text":"Mariska Hargitay's Olivia Benson is the longest-running regular character in US primetime live-action drama.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_%26_Order:_Special_Victims_Unit"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Law & Order","aliases":["Law order"],"value":"26 seasons","n":26,"article":"Law & Order","fact":{"text":"NBC brought it back in 2022 after an 11-year break, picking up with season 21.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_%26_Order"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Family Guy","aliases":["Familyguy","Faimly guy","Fam Guy","Famliy Guy","Family Guys"],"value":"25 seasons","n":25,"article":"Family Guy","fact":{"text":"Fox canceled it, then revived it in 2004 after strong DVD sales and reruns; it has aired ever since.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_Guy"}},{"rank":5,"name":"NCIS","aliases":["NCIS TV","Navy NCIS the TV Show","NCIS the show","Navy NCIS"],"value":"24 seasons","n":24,"article":"NCIS (TV series)","fact":{"text":"It began as two episodes of JAG in 2003 and was first titled Navy NCIS, which says \"Navy\" twice.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCIS_(TV_series)"}},{"rank":6,"name":"Grey's Anatomy","aliases":["Gray's Anatomy","Grey Anatomy","Greysanatomy","Greys natomy","Grey's","Greys Anatmy","Grace Anatomy","Grey′s Anatomy"],"value":"23 seasons","n":23,"article":"Grey's Anatomy","fact":{"text":"Its title mixes heroine Meredith Grey's surname with Gray's Anatomy, the classic anatomy textbook.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey%27s_Anatomy"}},{"rank":7,"name":"American Dad!","aliases":["Americandad"],"value":"22 seasons","n":22,"article":"American Dad!","fact":{"text":"The Smiths share their home with Roger, an alien, and Klaus, a goldfish.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Dad!"}},{"rank":8,"name":"Gunsmoke","aliases":["Gunsmoke TV Show"],"value":"20 seasons","n":20,"article":"Gunsmoke (TV series)","fact":{"text":"It began on radio in 1952 and ran 20 TV seasons and 635 episodes, the record until The Simpsons.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunsmoke_(TV_series)"}},{"rank":9,"name":"Lassie","aliases":["Timmy and Lassie"],"value":"19 seasons","n":19,"article":"Lassie (1954 TV series)","fact":{"text":"CBS dropped it partly because airing whole NFL games would push it out of its traditional 7 p.m. slot.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lassie_(1954_TV_series)"}},{"rank":10,"name":"Criminal Minds","aliases":[],"value":"19 seasons","n":19,"article":"Criminal Minds","fact":{"text":"It ended in 2020 after 15 seasons, then returned on Paramount+ in 2022 as Criminal Minds: Evolution.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Criminal_Minds"}}],"extras":[{"rank":11,"name":"Bob's Burgers","aliases":[],"value":"16 seasons","n":16},{"rank":12,"name":"CSI: Crime Scene Investigation","aliases":["CSI","Crime Scene Investigation"],"value":"15 seasons","n":15},{"rank":12,"name":"ER","aliases":[],"value":"15 s